dates payment v1
description "Closes on the 20th; pays on the 10th of the next month, or on the business day before when that day is closed. This version's example is wrong on purpose. The days are the example's own"
use calendar "office.cal"

inputs
  received : date  range >=2026-01-01 <=2026-10-31

date closing = received
  close day 20

date payment = closing
  day 10 of month +1
  roll preceding

examples
| received   | -> payment |
| 2026-04-01 | 2026-05-11 |
